# apps/site — environment variables the marketing site reads.
#
# Copy to apps/site/.env.local for local runs (that file is gitignored; only
# this .example is tracked). In production every value lives in Vercel →
# vantrow-outreach-site → Settings → Environment Variables (runbook 03 §3).
# Placeholders only: never a real value in this file.
#
# Every variable here is SERVER-ONLY: the site ships zero third-party scripts
# and reads nothing in the browser. Build-time (NEXT_PUBLIC_*) variables: none.
# With nothing set, the site runs: the early-access form falls back to a local
# file store outside production and answers 503 (never a silent success) in
# production.

# --- Early-access form storage (src/lib/waitlist.ts) ------------------------
# Both set → rows go to the Supabase `waitlist_signups` table (migration
# 0001; runbook 04).
# Otherwise: non-production writes .data/waitlist.jsonl (gitignored);
# production answers 503 waitlist_unconfigured.
# Project URL — Supabase → Settings → API.
SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# Service-role key (secret; bypasses RLS) — Supabase → Settings → API.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<from Supabase → Settings → API (service_role key); runbook 04>

# --- Founder notification on each signup (src/lib/notify.ts) ----------------
# Resend → API Keys. Optional: without it the notification is logged to the
# server console instead of sent.
RESEND_API_KEY=<from Resend → API Keys>
# Optional. Where the notification goes; defaults to the brand's supportEmail
# from @vantrow/brand.
ADMIN_NOTIFY_EMAIL=<address to notify, or leave unset>
# Optional. The From header; defaults to "<brand name> <supportEmail>". The
# domain must be verified in Resend.
MAIL_FROM=<Name <address@verified-domain>, or leave unset>

# --- Not set here ---------------------------------------------------------
# NODE_ENV — set by Next (`next dev` / `next build`); the code reads it to
#   pick the file store outside production and to silence the page-view stub's
#   console output in production. Do not set it in .env.local.
